        <h2 id="LDSChurch03">Church of Jesus Christ of Latter-day Saints</h2>
        <h3 id="PortfolioArchitect">Sr. Software Architect (Portfolio Architect)</h3>
        <p class="text-body-secondary">February 2026 – Present · Pathway Education portfolio</p>
        <p>I guide system architecture and technical direction for platforms that expand access to education globally, focusing on resilient, maintainable systems and alignment with organizational goals.</p>
        <p>
            My portfolio architecture work connects quality engineering, AI-assisted engineering, architecture governance,
            security, cloud modernization, and developer enablement across Global Education.
            <a asp-page="/Experience/EmploymentAccomplishments">Explore my employment accomplishments</a>
            for details on TAPIR, VISTA, Software Factory, enterprise AI architecture, and modernization work.
        </p>
        <h4 id="ArchitecturalDelivery">Selected architecture and product delivery</h4>
        <p>I have delivered full-stack production applications using the shared engineering resources below.
            My architectural work combines that production experience with reusable application foundations,
            automated validation, and practical developer tooling.</p>
        <ul class="resource-list">
            <li><strong>Shared full-stack application templates:</strong> Created reusable C#/.NET and Node.js/React
                foundations that combine ASP.NET Core APIs, Next.js clients, shared libraries, Aspire orchestration,
                authentication integration, caching, feature management, and telemetry.</li>
            <li><strong>Marketing website foundation:</strong> Built a focused ASP.NET Core and TypeScript/Next.js
                starter with feature-based boundaries, a defensive API proxy, reusable UI components, localization,
                design tokens, and automated unit, client, and browser validation.</li>
            <li><strong>QA automation framework:</strong> Served as the primary and nearly sole developer of a modular
                .NET framework for API, browser, data, and container-backed testing. Delivered reusable test lifecycles,
                multi-site and multi-browser execution, diagnostic capture, and isolated validation environments.</li>
            <li><strong>Developer toolbox:</strong> Developed shared local-development resources with Dev Containers,
                containerized services, cross-platform setup scripts, and reusable AI engineering guidance for
                GitHub Copilot, Codex, and Claude Code.</li>
            <li><strong>Integration and technology adoption:</strong> Implemented integrations between internal systems
                and Zendesk, developed API integrations and services, and provided technology reviews for adoption
                and implementation approval.</li>
        </ul>
        <h4>Technologies used in this architectural work</h4>
        <ul class="tag-list">
            <li>C# / .NET 10 / ASP.NET Core</li><li>Node.js / Next.js / React / TypeScript</li>
            <li>.NET Aspire</li><li>Tailwind CSS / Storybook / Zod</li>
            <li>NUnit / Selenium / Playwright / Vitest</li><li>Testcontainers / Docker / Podman</li>
            <li>OpenTelemetry / Seq / Application Insights / Dynatrace</li>
